<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korean Air H1 net loss narrows yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Korean Air H1 net loss narrows yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won, both loss)   2,700     vs  5,057</p>
<p>    Net loss		     134.42  vs    253.82</p>
<p>    Turnover		   1,946.05  vs  1,705.22</p>
<p>    Loss before tax	    134.42  vs    253.82</p>
<p>NOTE - Korean Air Lines Co, a unit of the Hanjin Group, is South Korea's biggest airline. The figures were released by the Korea Listed Companies Association.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
